      "proposed_content": "The Baez-Duarte and Jensen programs discretize completed-zeta information into different finite objects and retain different invariants: binomial reciprocal-zeta differences connect through an exponential generating function to a critical growth exponent, whereas coefficient windows form Jensen polynomials whose decisive invariant is real-rootedness and whose asymptotic analysis uses positive theta moments and local shift-ratio control.",
