    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_05e41860023a49bd66c80319c5e777ba7e0cd37f8d99c99f0ababb235a07e811",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Completion and functional equations provide reflection architecture but do not alone classify line-zero or Speiser equivalences: the Eisenstein source separates modular symmetry in z from spectral reflection in s without deriving a line-zero theorem, and the Speiser comparison reports both a positive modified-class extension and negative computational cases sharing the absence of a Riemann-type equation.",
