    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1bc71f421c7b87bb83578c6850b44a3632a0eae03fec1e36a98bcdef27b7b5dd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Robin-Lagarias and Nicolas-type criteria both package small-prime products into extremal arithmetic observables, but one-sided rates are decisive: Robin's incompatible RH and non-RH envelopes give a separated excess that eventually beats the elementary error, while the attempted Nicolas proof multiplies a known surplus by a factor with only a two-sided limiting value.",
