    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_81d0f67164651a77822918ffaaf83c11a4f5a2004b5d5eb6b80e2abccc2fc8be",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Changing a Nyman-Beurling dictionary is implication-specific: the antisymmetric difference dictionary preserves equivalence only because its missing fractional-part component is quantitatively restored, while generalized-kernel necessity needs no Mellin nonvanishing and compact-support sufficiency yields only zero-set inclusion until kernel-transform nonvanishing is added.",
